-- Two independent categorical experts compared by a BARE `==` (Bool result).
-- Semantically this is p(True) = Z = sum_k P_a(k) * P_b(k), the agreement
-- evidence of test/cases/neural/categoricalProductFusion -- and spelling the
-- same thing as `if v == w then True else False` compiles, takes the O(V)
-- agreement fusion, and answers 0.29 below. The bare spelling instead throws
-- "set-valued witness construction failed for the binding of 'v'".
-- Task bare-equality-of-two-neural-reads-crashes (found by the
-- lm-product-of-experts-decoding experiment).
neural camNN   :: (Symbol -> Int) of [0, 1, 2]
neural depthNN :: (Symbol -> Int) of [0, 1, 2]
main img depth =
  let v = camNN img in
  let w = depthNN depth in
  v == w
